**Topology:** Unity-gain Sallen-Key low-pass biquad, built around a two-stage Miller op-amp.

**Why a 2nd-order filter.** A 1st-order pole gives only about 20 dB at 10·fc, which is too close to the 19 dB requirement. A 2nd-order section with Q ≈ 0.6 has no passband peaking (peaking only starts above Q = 0.707). It gives about 36 dB at 10·fc.

**Setting the cutoff.**
- With equal resistors, Q = 0.5·√(C1/C2), so C1/C2 ≈ 1.44 gives Q = 0.6.
- With R1 = R2 = 100 kΩ, f0 = 1/(2π·R·√(C1·C2)) ≈ 41.6 kHz.
- For Q = 0.6, the -3 dB point is fc ≈ 0.827·f0 ≈ 34.4 kHz, near the middle of the 29.9–39 kHz window.
- Because the passives are ideal, fc and Q are set by R and C and should barely move across PVT. The op-amp only needs GBW well above f0·Q.

**Op-amp design.**
- **Input stage:** NMOS differential pair with a PMOS mirror load. The PMOS threshold (~1 V) is too high for a PMOS input pair at VCM = 0.9 V and VDD = 1.62 V. The NMOS pair is wide and long so it runs in weak inversion. That keeps Vgs low and leaves headroom for the long-L tail transistor even at ss / -40 °C.
- **Second stage:** PMOS common-source stage with an NMOS current sink. Compensation is Miller capacitance Cc in series with a nulling resistor Rz. GBW is roughly gm1/Cc, about 10 MHz or more.
- **Biasing:** IREF goes into a diode-connected NMOS, which is mirrored to the tail and the output sink. Assuming IREF ≈ 10 µA, the total current is about 40–50 µA, or under 100 µW at 1.98 V.
- **Polarity:** M1 (gate = vout) is the inverting input and M2 (gate = n2) is the non-inverting input. A rise at n2 pulls d2 down, which turns M5 on harder and raises vout.

```spice
.subckt dut vin vout vdd vss ibias
* ---- Sallen-Key unity-gain LPF ----
R1 vin n1 {R}
R2 n1 n2 {R}
C1 n1 vout {C1}
C2 n2 vss {C2}
* ---- bias ----
MB ibias ibias vss vss nfet W={WB} L={LB}
* ---- two-stage Miller op-amp: + = n2, - = vout ----
MT tail ibias vss vss nfet W={WT} L={LB}
M1 d1 vout tail vss nfet W={W1} L={L1}
M2 d2 n2   tail vss nfet W={W1} L={L1}
M3 d1 d1 vdd vdd pfet W={W3} L={L3}
M4 d2 d1 vdd vdd pfet W={W3} L={L3}
M5 vout d2 vdd vdd pfet W={W5} L={L3}
M6 vout ibias vss vss nfet W={W6} L={LB}
RZ d2 cz {RZ}
CC cz vout {CC}
.ends dut
```

