**Notes for the optimiser:**
- Keep C1/C2 ≈ 1.3–1.6 so that Q stays around 0.57–0.63. That keeps the margin on the 0.2 dB peaking limit and on the cutoff window.
- Two mirror ratios set the currents: WT/WB sets the tail current and W6/WB sets the output-stage current.
- Bias the output stage strongly enough to drive the R1/C1 feedback network and CL without slewing. That margin matters most at ss / 125 °C.
